cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the article under
  preferred-citation, and the archived data it reads under references.
title: >-
  b-free: analysis code for inferring Gutenberg-Richter earthquake size
  distributions without estimating b-values
abstract: >-
  Derivation, simulation and application code for the b-free estimators: a
  frequentist estimator that is unbiased for the earthquake size distribution
  of finite catalogs, rounded or not, and a Bayesian formulation giving
  closed-form posterior predictive size distributions. Includes the synthetic
  experiments, the application to the shallow area sources of the 2020
  European Seismic Hazard Model, the propagation through the hazard integral,
  and the figure pipeline for the manuscript.
type: software
